{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Line-anchor rot found and fixed while re-verifying the draft against the worktree at 9af88c3ada. Every file:line in the final ADR was machine-checked in range and spot-checked by content.\n\nROTTED, corrected:\n1. bedrock_model.py:88 'return BedrockProvider(region_name=region)' -> :101. :88 is now 'raise LLMConfigError('.\n2. bedrock_model.py:41-88 (build_bedrock_provider body) -> :41-101.\n3. bedrock_model.py:67-88 (region resolution) -> replaced with a symbol reference, since the range is now the tail of build_bedrock_provider.\n4. bedrock_model.py:78 (the Session().region_name preflight oracle) -> :87.\n5. completion_sidecar.py:213 -> :279.\n6. completion_sidecar.py:231 -> :297.\n7. capabilities.py _is_claude cited as :133-135 -> the def is at :121; now cited :121-135.\n8. docs/llm-framework.md stated as 666 lines -> it was 681 before my edits.\n9. The draft claimed llm-framework.md's 'trust-model section at :616-625 does not link out'. :616-625 is now the certifiable/AC-authoring material, not a trust-model section. Claim dropped.\n\nAMBIGUOUS, disambiguated: eight 'config.py:NNN' anchors (:117, :127, :159-160, :214-241, :244-261, :450-453, :463) all resolve correctly ONLY against src/rebar/llm/config.py; against the top-level src/rebar/config.py every one lands on unrelated text. Now qualified as llm/config.py, with an inline note.\n\nIMPRECISE, tightened: capabilities.py:457 was cited for 'dispatches SOLELY on prompt_cache_style' but is the def line; now cites the arms at :493 and :503. 'grep -rn netloc src/rebar' was said to return only structured_run.py:593 and gerrit_client.py; it also returns capabilities.py:428 (the rationale comment), now stated. 'first_class|best_effort' was said to appear only in capabilities.py across src/rebar; those tokens also occur in _cli/, _logging.py and outbound_differ.py for unrelated purposes, so the claim is now scoped to src/rebar/llm.\n\nVERIFIED STILL CORRECT (no change needed): all of capabilities.py's other anchors, providers.py, runner.py, structured.py, structured_run.py, failure.py, model_classes.py, iam.tf, iam_s7.tf, monitoring_s4b.tf, pyproject.toml, voter.py, the five test anchors, and llm-framework.md's :130-133 / :159-164 / :249-252 / :256 / :266-267 / :281-282. Also re-confirmed the zero-hit claims: _NATIVE_OUTPUT_PROVIDERS 0, force_prompted 0, cachePoint 0, botocore-config/aws_read_timeout 0, startswith in capabilities.py 0, bedrock in llm-framework.md 0 (before this change), bedrock in README.md 0.\n\nNote recorded in the ADR itself: check_comment_hygiene.py scans Python only, so a rotted anchor in a .md file has NO CI guard. The ADR therefore prefers symbol/section names wherever the sentence reads naturally either way."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785808757084717001,"uuid":"576132eb-9a2c-4ff7-8453-f6a185bb417d"}